OL,3,GNEWSAOne-way plan for 'pinch point'
OL,4,Astreet in Hull
OL,5,
OL,6,FResidents have welcomed plans to create
OL,7,Fa one-way system on a narrow street in
OL,8,FHull.
OL,10,FThey say Grafton Street, which runs
OL,11,Fbetween Newland Avenue and Beverley
OL,12,FRoad, is used as a cut-through and has
OL,13,Fproblems with safety and parking.
OL,15,FThe proposal would also see priority
OL,16,Ftraffic systems ` where road markings
OL,17,Findicate who should give way `
OL,18,Fintroduced to deal with "pinch points"
OL,19,Fon neighbouring De Grey Street, Lambert
OL,20,FStreet and Alexandra Road, if approved
OL,21,Fby Hull City Council in November.
OL,23,APub: 29-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
